==Old Norse==

===Etymology=== 
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*khrinda}}, akin to German {{term|Renn||reindeer|lang=de}} and Old English {{term|hran||reindeer|lang=ang}}, most likely from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ḱer-}}.

===Noun===
{{non-noun|m|hreins|hreinar}}

# [[reindeer]]

====Synonyms====
* {{l|non|hreindýri}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|non|hreindýri}}
* {{l|non|hreinbjálbi}}
* {{l|non|hreinstaka}}

